{"title":"Check If Point Is Reachable","difficulty":"Hard","statement":"There exists an infinitely large grid. You are currently at point (1, 1), and you need to reach the point (targetX, targetY) using a finite number of steps.\nIn one step, you can move from point (x, y) to any one of the following points:\n\n(x, y - x)\n(x - y, y)\n(2 * x, y)\n(x, 2 * y)\n\nGiven two integers targetX and targetY representing the X-coordinate and Y-coordinate of your final position, return true if you can reach the point from (1, 1) using some number of steps, and false otherwise.\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1\n\n```text\nInput: targetX = 6, targetY = 9\nOutput: false\n```\nExplanation: It is impossible to reach (6,9) from (1,1) using any sequence of moves, so false is returned.\n\n### Example 2\n\n```text\nInput: targetX = 4, targetY = 7\nOutput: true\n```\nExplanation: You can follow the path (1,1) -> (1,2) -> (1,4) -> (1,8) -> (1,7) -> (2,7) -> (4,7).\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 1 <= targetX, targetY <= 10^9","starterCode":"class Solution:\n    def isReachable(self, targetX: int, targetY: int) -> bool:\n        pass\n","entryPoint":"Solution().isReachable","parameters":[{"name":"targetX","type":"int"},{"name":"targetY","type":"int"}],"returnType":"bool","tests":[{"input":[1,1],"expected":true},{"input":[1000000000,1],"expected":true},{"input":[1000000000,1000000000],"expected":false},{"input":[104337989,67521412],"expected":false},{"input":[104346030,624625995],"expected":false},{"input":[105308856,105308857],"expected":true},{"input":[106034169,136369887],"expected":false},{"input":[106526992,106526996],"expected":true},{"input":[106871706,362533878],"expected":false},{"input":[106900960,442986970],"expected":false},{"input":[10699040,10699072],"expected":true},{"input":[108026500,108026502],"expected":true},{"input":[108134400,108265472],"expected":true},{"input":[108527616,109051904],"expected":true},{"input":[108963868,108963870],"expected":true},{"input":[113057792,113058816]